Z||000000||William Federle||08-20-2000||01:08 PM||||I don't think I've ever read exactly the Fiero Emergency brake works. Does the lever<BR>on the rear caliper act to lock hydraulic <BR>pressure after the brakes are applied and before they are released or does it mechanically force the pads to grip the rotor? <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-20-2000||01:16 PM||||It's completely mechanical. It uses a screw inside the caliper to clamp the rotor.||||reg||1
